From d6195d1e20234c224d47ebd17ee547f3f739c1b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pattex67 <33281022+pattex67@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:54:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] Yoshi: recheck rejected programs when their bytes
 change; TLD4.B 0x364 and uniform-handle gathers with an offset

- Lichii 46a184c4e3 (zortos293, branch diag/yoshi-reject-recheck): a rejected
  native program keeps the first 8 KiB it was made from and is read again at
  most every 250 ms; when the bytes changed it is lowered again. On by default
  for Yoshi and the Mysterious Book, which streams its shader code in (a
  program read before its code lands left draws or dispatches skipped);
  EDEN_NX2_REJECT_RECHECK=1 turns it on for every game, =0 off. Also for
  native compute programs already rejected.
- TLD4.B 0x364 (x, y | handle) and 0xf63 with an offset (handle then offset
  in the meta registers), from our earlier tree (7999db4eb2): Yoshi's chapter
  page and compute programs rejected them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h        |  36 ++++++-
 src/video_core/shader_cache.cpp               | 102 ++++++++++++++++--
 src/video_core/shader_cache.h                 |  14 ++-
 3 files changed, 140 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
